                <pb facs="0529" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">438.00/231: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-14T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14,
                                1923—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>47. For General Russell.</p>
                <p>Your April 3, 1 p.m., and April 12, 10 a.m. You may inform Haitian Government
                    that this Government considers that the jurisdiction of the Claims Commission
                    extends only to those claims pending on the date of the ratification of the
                    treaty. If the Haitian <pb facs="0530" n="406" xml:id="pg406"/> Government
                    concurs in this view the Department will notify those foreign governments whose
                    nationals have claims to submit to the Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
